          "path": "_m/s/x/6/v/uc-serefeli-mosque-wp/southwestern-minaret-u.jpg",
          "filename": "Uc Serefeli Mosque minaret DSCF4642.jpg",
          "caption": "The southwestern minaret of the Üç Şerefeli Mosque, Edirne, the tallest minaret in Turkey when it was built. The minaret was partly destroyed by an earthquake in 1752 and had to be reconstructed. The three balconies (which gave the mosque its name) were originally decorated with carved muqarnas but these were substituted for more Baroque-style curved rims or grooves during reconstruction. (See Kuban 2010, \"Ottoman Architecture\", p. 146 for info)",
